      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "No fixed release is available yet; update when Docker Hardened Images publishes one.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-6019: http.cookies Morsel.js_output() and BaseCookie.js_output() escape only double quotes in the inline <script> they return, so a cookie value containing </script> can break out of the script element. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/90309 (https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/76b3923d688c0efc580658476c5f525ec8735104), first released in CPython 3.13.14; no CPython 3.12 release carries the fix. See https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-6019. Checked Lib/http/cookies.py in the python-3.12 package of every build published in the DHI Alpine 3.23 repository, 3.12.12-r0 to 3.12.16-r4, x86_64 and aarch64; both architectures agree. Every published build ships the upstream js_output() that writes the cookie value into the script with only double quotes escaped, so every published build is affected."
    },
