      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-6019: http.cookies Morsel.js_output() and BaseCookie.js_output() escaped only double quotes in the inline <script> they return, so a cookie value containing </script> could break out of the script element. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/90309 (3.13 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/3c59b8b53fc75c7f9578d16fb8201ceb43e8f76c, which base64-encodes the value and decodes it with atob()), first released in CPython 3.13.14; a later 3.13 change, https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/149144, keeps the value encoded but switches to percent-encoding with decodeURIComponent(). See https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-6019. Checked Lib/http/cookies.py in the python-3.13 package of every build published in the DHI Alpine 3.23 repository, 3.13.12-r0 to 3.13.18-r4 (26 builds), x86_64 and aarch64; both architectures agree. 3.13.12-r0 to 3.13.13-r4 ship the upstream js_output() that writes the cookie value into the script with only double quotes escaped. From 3.13.13-r5, a DHI backport of the upstream change, js_output() base64-encodes the value and decodes it with atob(), and the 3.13.14 and later builds ship the upstream percent-encoding with decodeURIComponent(). The range ends at 3.13.13-r5."
    },
