      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-6019: http.cookies Morsel.js_output() (and so BaseCookie.js_output()) embedded the cookie value in an inline <script> element escaping only double quotes, so a value containing </script> could end the script element early. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/90309 (3.14 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/f795e042043dfe26c42e1971d4502c1cdc4c65b8, which base64-encodes the value), first released in CPython 3.14.5; CPython 3.14.6 replaced the base64 encoding with percent-encoding decoded by decodeURIComponent() (https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/4f17f6e04534d93fbd23862f9f290d3a281ab30b), which also escapes < and /. See https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/IVNWGV2BBNC3RHQAFS22UP4DY56SAXX3/ and https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-6019. Checked js_output() in Lib/http/cookies.py in every published build of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.14 package, 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.10-r4, on x86_64 and aarch64; both architectures agree. 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.4-r4 embed the value with only double quotes escaped. 3.14.4-r5 is the first build with the fix, a DHI backport of the upstream base64 change to CPython 3.14.4, and 3.14.4-r6 to 3.14.5-r9 keep it; 3.14.6-r9 and every later build ship the percent-encoded form. The range ends at 3.14.4-r5."
