      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-6019: http.cookies Morsel.js_output() and BaseCookie.js_output() escape only double quotes in the inline <script> they return, so a cookie value containing </script> can break out of the script element. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/90309 (https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/76b3923d688c0efc580658476c5f525ec8735104), first released in CPython 3.13.14; no CPython 3.12 release carries the fix. See https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-6019. Checked Lib/http/cookies.py in the standard library shipped by these packages (libpython-3.12-stdlib and libpython-3.12-minimal) in every build published in the DHI Debian repository, 3.12.13-0 to 3.12.16-7, amd64 and arm64; both architectures agree. From 3.12.16-5, js_output() base64-encodes the cookie value and decodes it with atob() in the script, a backport of the upstream change; 3.12.13-0 to 3.12.16-4 ship the upstream file without it. The range ends at 3.12.16-5."
